{"entryId":"1802","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1802:1","sourceSha256":"fe946722fa048a2f3521f4ac6d5dfd6d83d76a6bfd636ca17705fa8af7b4a872","englishSha256":"0b7c9924984ed3862bb8076a6ca1f42bc65856d0878625999b28ae331d6d58fe","citations":[{"id":"1802:1:link-01","he":[8,85],"en":[11,24],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_16b.15"},"reference":"Kiddushin 16b:15","assessment":"The Bavli gives Rav Yosef and Rashi explains expansion from the small letter yod into a large city as unnecessary proliferation.","evidence":[{"reference":"Kiddushin 16b:15","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_16b.15"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rashi on Kiddushin 16b:15:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Kiddushin_16b.15.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"1802:1:link-02","he":[87,104],"en":[115,124],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sefer_HeArukh%2C_Letter_Yod_21"},"reference":"Sefer HeArukh, Letter Yod 21","assessment":"The checked Arukh first supplies the same wordplay and then transmits a Gaon’s sage-name explanation. Keep the two voices and reported Arukh summary.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sefer HeArukh, Letter Yod 21","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sefer_HeArukh%2C_Letter_Yod_21"},"witness":"Sefer HeArukh, Lublin 1883"}]},{"id":"1802:1:link-03","he":[168,197],"en":[282,298],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ritva_on_Kiddushin_16b.6"},"reference":"Ritva on Kiddushin 16b:6","assessment":"The actual Ritva gives Rashi’s reading, his wordplay and Raavad’s alternative. Its preference is attached to the interpretation just quoted.","evidence":[{"reference":"Ritva on Kiddushin 16b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ritva_on_Kiddushin_16b.6"},"witness":"Chiddushei haRitva, Munkatch, 1908."}]},{"id":"1802:1:link-04","he":[293,316],"en":[618,651],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Taanit_24a.2"},"reference":"Taanit 24a:2","assessment":"The named intermediary, Ritva, directly preserves this attribution and connects it to the harsh man in Taanit. This does not identify the Raavad’s exact original gloss.","evidence":[{"reference":"Taanit 24a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Taanit_24a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Ritva on Kiddushin 16b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ritva_on_Kiddushin_16b.6"},"witness":"Chiddushei haRitva, Munkatch, 1908."}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,3],"holds":[{"raw":"ובשס\"ח בגליון פי' גאון יוד קרת שם עיר","reason":"Hafla’ah records the Geonic town-name explanation as a marginal reading. The exact Talmud edition and its margin remain to collate. The Arukh also has a different Geonic interpretation.","evidence":[{"reference":"Hafla'ah ShebaArakhin on Sefer HeArukh, Letter Yod 6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Hafla%27ah_ShebaArakhin_on_Sefer_HeArukh%2C_Letter_Yod_6"},"witness":"Sefer HeArukh, Lublin 1883"},{"reference":"Sefer HeArukh, Letter Yod 21","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sefer_HeArukh%2C_Letter_Yod_21"},"witness":"Sefer HeArukh, Lublin 1883"}]},{"raw":"אבל הראב\"ד גורס אמר רבה","reason":"The Ritva transmits the Raavad reading. The original Raavad witness remains to locate.","evidence":[{"reference":"Ritva on Kiddushin 16b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ritva_on_Kiddushin_16b.6"},"witness":"Chiddushei haRitva, Munkatch, 1908."},{"reference":"Taanit 24a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Taanit_24a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"The texts give small-letter wordplay, a sage’s name, a town name and the analogy to a severe person. Preserve the distinct attributions and Ritva’s reported Raavad reading.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Kiddushin 16b:15","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_16b.15"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rashi on Kiddushin 16b:15:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Kiddushin_16b.15.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Sefer HeArukh, Letter Yod 21","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sefer_HeArukh%2C_Letter_Yod_21"},"witness":"Sefer HeArukh, Lublin 1883"},{"reference":"Hafla'ah ShebaArakhin on Sefer HeArukh, Letter Yod 6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Hafla%27ah_ShebaArakhin_on_Sefer_HeArukh%2C_Letter_Yod_6"},"witness":"Sefer HeArukh, Lublin 1883"},{"reference":"Ritva on Kiddushin 16b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ritva_on_Kiddushin_16b.6"},"witness":"Chiddushei haRitva, Munkatch, 1908."},{"reference":"Taanit 24a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Taanit_24a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
